OL,3,GNEWSAStar Trek offers 'optimistic view
OL,4,Aof the future'
OL,5,
OL,6,FA man from East Kent with an enduring
OL,7,Flove for all things Star Trek said the
OL,8,Ftelevision series offered an
OL,9,F"optimistic view of the future" in an
OL,10,Fincreasingly "dystopian world".
OL,12,FAs Star Trek celebrates 60 years since
OL,13,Ffirst gracing our screens, it has huge
OL,14,Fnumbers of devoted disciples. Arguably,
OL,15,Ffewer are more dedicated than James
OL,16,FDillon.
OL,18,FDillon, who is a regular at fan
OL,19,Fconventions for which he builds Star
OL,20,FTrek sets, believes this hobby offers
OL,21,Fhis life balance.
OL,23,APub: 08-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,322,320,200,140,0,100
